Scope (owner decision 2026-10-15): the performance remainder only. Four of the card's seven goals landed
early (#107/#109/#123, `ShapeRange`). Streaming save is dropped unless the lazy-blob measurement shows that
save, not load, holds the memory. Cross-run text stays v0.7.0.

## Goals
- Lazy binary blobs: image and media parts (and other binary parts) keep a reference into the
  package zip and read their bytes only when `.blob` is first accessed. Today every part's bytes are
  read when the deck loads.
- Caching audit: review all 206 `@lazyproperty` uses (47 files) for soundness, meaning no stale
  value after a mutation the API allows. Add a cache only where a hot path recomputes a derived
  collection, and only with a measured win (#51 showed `paragraphs`/`runs` caching is a loss).

## Objectives / acceptance
- Memory: `tracemalloc` peak for opening a 100-image deck, before and after, recorded in
  `.claude/context/performance.md`; open-then-save stays byte-identical for untouched binary parts.
- Every caching-audit finding is fixed with a failing-first test, or recorded as sound with a reason.
- `tests/perf` baseline re-run at branch close: no tracked operation slower than its baseline;
  the work-count gate passes without raising its budget.
- Full suite green; `tests/perf` under 60 s on CI.
- Card `.meta/roadmap/stages/03-hardening-and-gaps/v0.6.0.md` expanded with implementation detail
  before code lands.
